# What a CLI deploy must never upload.
#
# `npm run deploy` is `vercel --prod`, which uploads the working directory —
# tracked or not. Without this file that included the 83 untracked files under
# app/, among them a live GCP service-account private key
# (firebase-adminsdk-fbsvc-intrep@intrepid-stage-495117-q1) and app/shared/.env.local.
# Git-driven deploys were never affected; only a deploy run from a laptop.
#
# Keep this list ahead of the app/ tree being tidied, not behind it: the guard
# should hold even if someone re-creates one of these directories later.
app/
archive/
.vercel/
_shared/reports/
Devices/
Server/
Database/backups/
*.log

# Local env files, wherever they turn up.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Heavy local-only trees. A CLI deploy from the laptop must never upload these;
# Git-driven deploys already skip them via .gitignore, but .vercelignore
# overrides .gitignore for `vercel --prod`, so without this the upload tries to
# push ~28 GB (runs/ alone is 26 GB) and hangs indefinitely.
runs/
.venv/
venv/
vscode-office/
node_modules/
.deepsec/
scratch/
personal_folder_agent/
permanent_agent/
jpbir/
.firebase/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.qwen/
.kiro/
.agents/
.claude/

# Untracked workspace-only files and directories at the repository root.
# In particular, never send service-account JSON or one-off Firestore tools.
.firebaserc
Sandbox/
chrome_extraction/
dashboard/
dataconnect/
eka-runner-private/
eka-runner/
jayti/
_tmp_*
intrepid-stage-*.json
firestore-queue-cleanup-*.json
hash_output.txt
STATUS_SUMMARY.txt
stale_db_inventory.md
stale_db_refs.txt
*_REPORT.md
*_SUMMARY.md
*_COMPLETE.md
*_GUIDE.md
*_PLAN.md
*_PROGRESS.md
WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY_MAP.md
REMAINING_REFS_ANALYSIS.md
SAFE_TO_DELETE_FILES.md
yarn.lock
